ed object. Whenever that objec\t is selected, and the Script Editing box is popped up, the associated s\cript will be loaded into the box.)/Dest (G8.877352)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23872 0 R >> endobj23872 0 obj<< /Title (7. Click on the Apply button. This associates the script with the select\ed object. If there is an error in your script, a Messages box will appe\ar describing the prob lem.)/Dest (G8.878794)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23873 0 R /Next 23871 0 R >> endobj23873 0 obj<< /Title (6. Open the Functions pulldown menu to insert XDrawMaker functions into \your script. When you click on a function name, it will be inserted into\ the script at the insertion point, with dummy arguments which you need \to replace with the ap pro...)/Dest (G8.877348)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23874 0 R /Next 23872 0 R >> endobj23874 0 obj<< /Title (5. Enter the location of the event. Possible locations are:)/Dest (G8.877326)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23875 0 R /Next 23873 0 R >> endobj23875 0 obj<< /Title (4. Click on the name of the event you want to launch the script for the \selected ob ject. The script format will be displayed.)/Dest (G8.877320)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23876 0 R /Next 23874 0 R >> endobj23876 0 obj<< /Title (3. Open the Actions menu by clicking on that item in the box.)/Dest (G8.877318)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23877 0 R /Next 23875 0 R >> endobj23877 0 obj<< /Title (2. Open the Script Editing box by clicking on Activate/Script.)/Dest (G8.877316)/Parent 23869 0 R /Prev 23870 0 R /Next 23876 0 R >> endobj23878 0 obj<< /Title (4.6 Grids and View Options)/Dest (G7.427155)/Parent 23547 0 R /Prev 23880 0 R /Next 23868 0 R /First 23881 0 R /Last 23882 0 R /Count 8 >> endobj23879 0 obj<< /Title (CHAPTER 5: Animating a Drawing)/Dest (G8.877260)/Parent 23868 0 R >> endobj23880 0 obj<< /Title (4.5 Cut, Copy, Paste, Duplicate, Delete)/Dest (G7.427135)/Parent 23547 0 R /Prev 23889 0 R /Next 2